%description:

Tcp.windowAutoTuning:no-buffer -- auto-tuning without a receive buffer stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "needs receiveBufferSize, else an error".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true, the value of LinuxTcp), no-buffer (true
without receiveBufferSize: an error). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() sets
the offer and the clamp, half the buffer, and checks the buffer; each data segment grows the
offer by max(2 * MSS, 2 * its length) up to the clamp (TcpConnection::processSegment1stThru8th()).

Host under test: host2, without receiveBufferSize. Observation: the error, and the exit code of
the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowAutoTuning
%# class: no-buffer
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowAutoTuningNoBuffer compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning = true    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
windowAutoTuning needs a receive buffer, but receiveBufferSize is not set
